WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.870
The word euthanasia comes from Greek.

2
00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:04.950
It means good death.

3
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.210
In the Netherlands and Belgium,
it has been legal since 2002.

4
00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:12.880
In England and Wales,
assisting suicide is a crime,

5
00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:15.910
under the Suicide Act 1961.

6
00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:21.160
In 2025, MPs voted for a
bill to allow assisted dying.

7
00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:25.730
In 2026 it ran out of time
and did not become law.

8
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:31.090
So if someone is dying and in pain,
is helping them die an act of mercy,

9
00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:32.590
or of killing?

10
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.960
In this mission, you'll sort
out the kinds of euthanasia:

11
00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:39.400
active and passive, voluntary and not.

12
00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.670
Then you'll see what
Christian teaching says,

13
00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:44.620
and weigh up whether
the law should change.

14
00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:49.870
Your mission: weigh up whether helping
someone die is mercy or killing.
